course: dictionary
lesson: 2998
title: Dung: a word from nature
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Dung is a plain, scientific word for animal poo, and you can work out its meaning from the words around it. «A horned dung beetle was measured pulling about 1,141 times its own weight.» Beetle is an animal, and the clues about pulling and weight do not tell you what dung is, so look at the sentence about the beetle that rolls it: «Dung beetles roll balls of dung, bury it and lay eggs in it.» Rolling, burying and laying eggs in something tells you dung is what an animal leaves behind.
explain: Always check by swapping in your meaning. «Dung beetles roll balls of poo, bury it and lay eggs in it.» That still makes sense, so you have got it right. Dung is a polite word, not a rude one, which is why it is used in science and history lessons.
explain: Context also tells you what dung can be used for. «Camels save water by making dry dung.» «In places with little wood, dried dung is burned for cooking and heating.» Burned for cooking and heating are clues that dried dung can be fuel, something that gives heat when it burns.
fact: Dung means the solid waste, or poo, of animals, especially large animals like cows, horses and elephants.
fact: A «dung beetle» rolls dung into balls, buries it and lays its eggs in it.
fact: «Cow dung» is the dung of cows, and a «dung heap» is a pile of it.
fact: Dung is used on farms as manure to help plants grow.
fact: In some places dung is dried and burned as fuel, especially where there is little wood.
exercise: «The dung beetle rolled a ball of dung up the tunnel.» What is dung? | *Animal poo | A type of dry grass | A small stone | Wet mud from the river
exercise: «Dried dung is burned for cooking and heating where there is little wood.» What is dried dung used for? | To make a soft bed | *As fuel, to cook and heat | To hang on the wall | To make bread rise
exercise: Nadia says dung is a rude word. Is she right? | Yes, it is a rude word that you should never say | *No, it is a polite, scientific word used in science lessons
test: Farmers spread dung on their fields. Why do they do this? | To keep the rain away | *To help plants grow | To hide the field from the cows | To make the fields smell nice
test: «Dung beetles roll balls of dung, bury it and lay eggs in it.» What do dung beetles do with dung? | They burn it to make light | *They roll it into balls and bury it | They eat it all in one bite | They sell it at the market
exam: «Camels save water by making dry dung, and they can drink up to 100 litres at once.» What does dung mean here? | A type of camel food | Dry grass for eating | Water stored in the hump | *Animal poo
